BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Photo Editing and Management with Adobe Lightroom Classic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T160000
UID:6a187c11703c3363002a94df@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Lightroom Classic is an industry standard tool used by p
 hotographers to organize\, retouch\, their work. We will focus on learning
  the workflow of the software\, covering topics such as importing photos\,
  file organization\, retouching and correcting our images\, and exporting 
 and sharing our finished work.\nRegistration is required.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a187c11703c3363002a94df
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Adobe Illustrator
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T193000
UID:6a270d8390cc4e3a790c88aa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Illustrator is the industry-standard software for creati
 ng vector graphics and illustrations\, and is used for logo design\, brand
 ing\, typography\, and digital artwork.\nJoin us for an introductory lesso
 n and discover the essential tools used to bring ideas to life! We’ll ex
 plore the Illustrator workspace and learn how to create and edit shapes\, 
 paths\, colour\, text\, and more. You’ll also get to create a design fro
 m scratch. Whether you're a beginner or looking to brush up on your skills
 \, this event is perfect for anyone interested in design.\nRegistration is
  required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, 2nd floor Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a270d8390cc4e3a790c88aa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T160000
UID:6a187c74f56bd86e00b2c580@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a187c74f56bd86e00b2c580
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Virtual Reality Demo for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T170000
UID:6a354fbf154fb14b002264d5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This Drop-In demonstration is for patrons over the age of 13 y
 ears old.\nLeap into the world of virtual reality at the library! Join thi
 s drop-in session to try out the Meta Quest virtual reality headset and im
 merse  yourself in stunning 360-degree environments\, engage in captivatin
 g  adventures\, and interact with the virtual world.
LOCATION:Daniel G. Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a354fbf154fb14b002264d5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North York Central Library Film Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T160000
UID:6a32ee4f2ea730c17ab7a808@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an afternoon screening of "The Fantastic 4:
  First Steps".\nThe Fantastic 4:\nFirst Steps\n(2025)\nRunning time: 115 m
 inutes\nDirector: Matt Shakman\nStarring: Pedro Pascal\, Vanessa Kirby\, E
 bon Moss-Bachrach\, Joseph Quinn\, and Julia Garner\nSet against the vibra
 nt backdrop of a 1960s-inspired\, retro-futuristic world\, Marvel's First 
 Family is introduced as they face a daunting challenge. Forced to balance 
 their roles as heroes with the strength of their family bond\, the Fantast
 ic Four must defend Earth from a ravenous space god called Galactus and hi
 s enigmatic herald\, the Silver Surfer.\nThe North York Central Library Fi
 lm Club meets monthly on Wednesdays. There is a short\, informal discussio
 n after the screening\, time permitting.\nRegistration is not required. Pl
 ease contact the Browsery Department at 416-395-5672 for more information.
 \nNext dates:\nSeptember 16 (Wednesday\, at 2 PM): TBA
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nf Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32ee4f2ea730c17ab7a808
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
