BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to 3D Printing & Design with Tinkercad
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T113000
UID:6a393a808d1b82ca9f7b9cea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A hands-on workshop where participants will learn how 3D Print
 ing works and use Tinkercad to explore 3D design basics.\nNew to 3D Printi
 ng and Design? Come and watch and learn from TPL Staff on how a 3D printer
  works in the Digital Innovation Hub.\nClass instruction includes:\nHow to
  prepare a 3D design file for print\nHow to use the equipment properly and
  safely\nReviewing the rules and guidelines to using the 3D printer\nFollo
 wed by the introduction to printing\, class participants will be given a h
 ands-on workshop where they learn how to create simple 3D designed key cha
 in and become familiar with design tools.\nRegistration is required for th
 is class. You can order free tickets by clicking the link below. Tickets w
 ill become available one week prior to the class at 9 a.m.\nIt is strongly
  recommended that you create at Tinkercad.com ahead of the session.\nInfor
 mation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collec
 ted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, section
 s 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event a
 nd program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the
  library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\n
 answerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
 .
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a393a808d1b82ca9f7b9cea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
