DESCRIPTION:Toronto Public Library is preparing plans to relocate and exp
 and its Woodside Square branch. The new branch will remain in the Woodside
  Square Mall at 1571 Sandhurst Circle\, in a larger renovated unit and off
 er expanded space and services - and we’d like your input.\nJoin Librar
 y staff\, Councillor Jamaal Myers and Ken Fukushima Architects for a con
 sultation to hear about the Woodside Square branch’s relocation and exp
 ansion project.\nAt the session\, there will be:\nA presentation providin
 g an overview of the Woodside Square branch's relocation and expansion pro
 ject\, including key updates\, design considerations and next steps\;\nOpp
 ortunities to share your feedback on what you’d like to see in the new s
 pace\, to learn about future engagement opportunities and how you can con
 tinue to participate throughout the project\;\nA live Q&A with project sta
 ff.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe Personal Information on this form
  is collection by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
