BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Let's Learn About Computer Hardware
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260727T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T173000
UID:6a19cf5fbd892a0672e64c0d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This hands-on workshop series introduces the process of buildi
 ng a gaming desktop\, from selecting components to installing an operating
  system. Participants will disassemble a desktop to learn about internal h
 ardware and basic troubleshooting. The series also covers OS selection and
  installation\, along with essential cybersecurity tips using open-source 
 tools.\nThis workshop is run by Free Geek Toronto.\nThis program is part o
 f Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after scho
 ol and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nu
 tritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor 
 call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a19cf5fbd892a0672e64c0d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Create a Video Game Concept
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T113000
UID:6a3ac56b40f004e45f8572d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in what makes a video game? Join us for this lectur
 e by TMU Professor Fitzgerald\, and learn where to start when designing 
 a video game\,  from mechanics to player experience.\nChildren under 13 m
 ust be accompanied by an adult.\nRegistration begins June 27th\, 2026 at 1
