BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Asefeh Katoozian
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T235959
UID:6a469df04407827f8aa8e2f2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July the works of Asefeh Katoozian are
  on display at Morningside branch\nAsefeh is a multidisciplinary artist an
 d architect with an interest in philosophy. Her work explores painting thr
 ough rhythm\, form\, structure\, and visual language\, focusing on the rel
 ationship between composition and perception. She transforms visual elemen
 ts into expressive forms that create a dialogue between nature\, memory\, 
 and movement. Her practice reflects an ongoing exploration of how visual e
 xperience shapes meaning\, perception\, and inner understanding.\nI explor
 e rhythm\, form\, structure\, and light as guiding elements of artistic ex
 pression in my practice. The relationship between these elements creates s
 pace for introspection and imagination. Through this practice\, I shape co
 mpositions that investigate how rhythm\, light\, and the Persian alphabet 
 influence my inner journey in the process of creating an artwork.\nThis ex
 hibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit program\n. Toronto Public Library prov
 ides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the
  city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the
  city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during Morningsid
 e's open hours. Please check the\nMorningside Branch\npage before your vi
 sit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nTitle of Piece: Rhythm Ink on the Paper 19.5
  * 24.5 Credit: Asefeh Katoozian
LOCATION:Morningside
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a469df04407827f8aa8e2f2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
