END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Your Library Soundtrack: AI and Music Production Closing Showcase
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T160000
UID:6a3e859118f4729377196193@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Over the past 12 weeks\, participants in TPL's Innovator in Re
 sidence (AI and Music Production) program have been exploring how artifici
 al intelligence can enhance and amplify their own music creativity. They'v
 e learned that rather than making music for you\, AI can offer you new way
 s to develop and realize original ideas\, regardless of music experience. 
 They've also learned how to use these tools responsibly\, including how to
  navigate the ethical considerations that come with AI-generated music.\nJ
 oin us for the closing celebration of Innovator in Residence Joel S. Silve
 r's spring residency at Fairview's Digital Innovation Hub. We will share s
 ome of the AI-assisted musical work from residency participants - original
  pieces shaped by their own creative vision and brought to life with the h
 elp of AI tools. Joel will also debut his own Library Soundtrack and intro
 duce a free online resource created during the residency - a guide to ever
 y lesson covered over the 12 weeks\, complete with step-by-step instructio
 ns so that anyone can continue exploring AI-assisted music production on t
 heir own. Come hear what's possible when human creativity and artificial i
 ntelligence meet - and when human expression remains at the core of all ar
 t.\nThis program is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and Music Produ
 ction) program\, which is designed to help beginner and intermediate learn
 ers build knowledge and creative skills and get hands-on with current AI t
 ools in music production and learn about the history\, copyright and ethic
 s of generative music. For more information and a full list of programs\, 
 visit\ntpl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e859118f4729377196193
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
