BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Teen Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260725T150000
UID:6a0f7959f56bd86e00b13cff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Morningside library's Teen Book Club! Come join us every other
  month to discuss an exciting book in a fun & friendly atmosphere! Light r
 efreshments will be available. All teens & youth are welcome!\nThe next Te
 en Book Club is on SAT JULY 25 (2-3pm) & the book we will discuss is\nI Ho
 pe You Get This Message\nby Farah Naz Rishi.\nIn June\, copies of the book
  will be available at Morningside branch - feel free to come by & borrow a
  copy at your convenience - or place a hold on your own\, if you prefer.\n
 Information Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is c
 ollected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, se
 ctions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for ev
 ent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about ho
 w the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff
  at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4
 W 2G8.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0f7959f56bd86e00b13cff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Watercolour Trees and Chickens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T160000
UID:6a0f848d43b41b3d00683a94@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, participants will learn a few basic waterco
 lour techniques while having fun making their paintings. We will be colour
  mixing to make fun little chickens and learning the salt technique to pai
 nt a beautiful tree in winter scene. some of the techniques we will be exp
 loring are: colour mixing\, wet on wet\, salt technique. This will be a fu
 n two-in-one workshop that is perfect for any level.\nMaterials will be p
 rovided. This program is for teens.\nYou can register online or drop-in 
 while space allows.\n​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0f848d43b41b3d00683a94
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
