BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Clicker Fidget Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T173000
UID:6a35a19edcc1022f003a2ab2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub to make your own customized clicker f
 idgets! In this workshop\, you’ll learn how to add your own custom text 
 to your clicker using PrusaSlicer. Then while those are printed\, you’ll
  get to choose from a variety of clicker fidget designs to paint and make 
 your own. All materials will be provided.\nThis program is part of Youth H
 ub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in
  the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious
  snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call th
 e branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a35a19edcc1022f003a2ab2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Henna Art Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T150000
UID:6a35b6dfdcc1022f003a2b97@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This henna art program will offer participants the opportunity
  to create their own unique henna designs. Through guided instruction\, pa
 rticipants learn about the history and cultural significance of henna\, as
  well as techniques for creating intricate patterns. Participants are enco
 uraged to explore their creativity and design their own patterns\, which t
 hey then apply using henna paste. Presented by Fathima Asma Saheel. For te
 ens.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Annette Street\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a35b6dfdcc1022f003a2b97
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Employment Summer Workshop for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T170000
UID:6a160428c6a1dc3d00d63f5e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Canadian Training Institute is thrilled to present a two- 
 day series that will introduce participants to employment and job search s
 kills for future success Topics will include:\nResume Basics\nJob Search S
 trategies\nInterview Skills and Preparation\nVolunteer hours can be provid
 ed to participants upon completion of the camp.\nPlease note that this pro
 gram is for teens ages 13-17 only.
LOCATION:Fairview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a160428c6a1dc3d00d63f5e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
