BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Bars & Beats: Studying the Poetry Behind Rap
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T170000
UID:6a3ab65a7550c8bf9f5f4b18@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, led by Coach Desiree McKenzie\, participant
 s will explore the global and local roots of spoken word\, specifically ex
 amining how rap music utilizes poetic tools like rhythm\, metaphor\, and s
 torytelling.\nThe goal of this program is to help participants recognize r
 ap as poetry in motion\, examine lyrics analytically\, and create original
  spoken word pieces inspired by musical flow and technique.\nThis is an in
  person drop-in program for teens 13 -17.\nThis program is part of Youth H
 ub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in
  the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious
  snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call th
 e branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Woodside Square
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3ab65a7550c8bf9f5f4b18
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Scale Model Kit Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T163000
UID:6a3ac43c7550c8bf9f5f4f5a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build and customize your own scale model kit! Choose from Gund
 am models\, plant-themed kits\, and popular animation character kits. Lear
 n basic assembly techniques\, add your personal touch\, and bring your cre
 ation to life. No experience needed—all skill levels welcome. While supp
 lies last.\nThis is an in person drop-in program for teens 13 -17.\nThis p
 rogram is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for 
 teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always avai
 lable. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with
  a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Woodside Square
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3ac43c7550c8bf9f5f4f5a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T153000
UID:6a3acaed4407827f8aa6def4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this course you will learn how python code works and given time to p
 ractice. Prior coding knowledge is not necessary for this introductory cla
 ss. Key takeaways will include a working knowledge of variables\, loops\, 
 conditional arguments and more.\nRegistration is required.\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Center 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3acaed4407827f8aa6def4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
